<title>SOUTH KOREA: US Unit of Hyundai in $1.1 bln deal with NetHold.</title>
<headline>US Unit of Hyundai in $1.1 bln deal with NetHold.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. subsidiary of South Korea's Hyundai Electronics Industries Co Ltd said on Tuesday it has won a $1.1 billion won order from Dutch-based NetHold to supply digital satellite broadcasting receivers.  </p>
<p>A Hyundai Electronics America statement said it would start providing the receivers for five years starting late 1996.</p>
<p>NetHold, which provides pay TV services to Europe, Africa and the Middle East, will supply the receivers to Europe and Africa, it said.</p>
<p>The statement said Hyundai Electronics forecast a turnover of $300 million from the digital receiver sector in 1997.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
